description:
Yamas = ethical restraints or social disciplines:
1. Ahimsa – non-violence;
2. Satya – truthfulness;
3. Asteya – non-stealing;
4. Brahmacharya – moderation;
5. Aparigraha – non-possessiveness.

1. Mitra → Friend, friendly;
2. Ravi → Sun, shining one;
3. Sūrya → Sun, all-pervading;
4. Bhānu / Bhānav → Illuminator, radiance;
5. Khaga → Sky-traveler, moving across the sky;
6. Pūṣa → Nourisher, sustainer;
7. Hiraṇyagarbha → Golden womb, cosmic source;
8. Mārīci → Ray, originator of light;
9. Āditya → Son of Aditi, Sun deity;
10. Savitr → Creative, life-producer;
11. Arka → Brightener, that which illuminates;
12. Bhaskara → All-enlightening, light-maker.
